# Local frontend refresh

After finishing frontend work in **ord-frontend**, reload generated artifacts or the dev server when changes require it:

```bash
make refresh   # paraglide + svelte-kit sync (i18n, routes)
make wipe      # refresh + clear .svelte-kit cache
```

## When to refresh

| Change | Action |
|--------|--------|
| `messages/source/**` | `make refresh`; restart dev server if running |
| Routes / `+page` / `app.html` | `make refresh` |
| Env / `.env` | Restart dev server (`ord-ops make dev-up` or `bun run dev`) |

## Tests and CI

```bash
make ci          # after most code changes
make ci-e2e      # after E2E flow changes (requires ord-ops: make e2e-up)
make test-e2e    # Playwright on e2e stack (ord-ops: make e2e-up)
make test-dev    # Playwright on dev stack (ord-ops: make dev-up)
```

## Backend stack

**Never** start or manage the backend from ord-frontend. Use **ord-ops**:

- Dev stack: `cd ../ord-ops && make dev-up`
- E2E stack: `cd ../ord-ops && make e2e-up`
- Native API: `cd ../ord-ops && make api-run` / `make api-restart`
